// Title: Suspicious SYSVOL Domain Group Policy Access
// Sigma ID: 05f3c945-dcc8-4393-9f3d-af65077a8f86
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Markus Neis, Jonhnathan Ribeiro, oscd.community
// Date: 2018-04-09 | Modified: 2022-01-07
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1552.006
// Description: Detects Access to Domain Group Policies stored in SYSVOL
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity
// References:
//   - https://adsecurity.org/?p=2288
//   - https://www.hybrid-analysis.com/sample/f2943f5e45befa52fb12748ca7171d30096e1d4fc3c365561497c618341299d5?environmentId=100
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_sysvol_access.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\SYSVOL\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\policies\\"
